BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE REGENT OF MUSI RAWAS UTARA,

Considering : a. that all forms of violence, torture or treatment that degrades the dignity and honor of women and children constitute violations of human rights, therefore it is necessary to protect their honor and dignity and guarantee their right to life in accordance with their nature and destiny without discrimination;

b. that violence, torture or treatment that degrades the dignity and honor of women and children continues to increase so that protection efforts must be undertaken;

c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a and b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women and Children;

In view of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 16 of 2013 concerning the Establishment of Musi Rawas Utara Regency in South Sumatra Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2013 Number 112, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5429);

3. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic

of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587), as amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);

With the Joint Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF MUSI RAWAS UTARA REGENCY and

THE REGENT OF MUSI RAWAS UTARA

HAS DECIDED:

To enact: REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING THE ADMINISTRATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN.

Part Two Parents and Family

Article 27

Parents and Family are obliged and responsible to:

a. nurture, care for, and educate Children;
b. develop Children according to their abilities, talents, and interests;
c. prevent marriage at Child age;
d. provide character education and instill moral values in Children.
e. prevent violations of the rights of Women and Children; and
f. protect Women and Children from acts of violence.

Article 5

(1) Every Woman has the right to:

a. embrace a religion and worship according to her religion and belief;
b. obtain education, benefit from science and technology, arts and culture, in order to improve the quality of her life;
c. live and sustain life and her livelihood;
d. form a family and continue her lineage through lawful marriage;
e. develop herself and advance herself;
f. work and receive fair and proper remuneration and treatment in employment relations;
g. obtain equal opportunity in law and government;
h. freedom of association, assembly and expression of opinion;
i. protection of personal self, family, honor, dignity and property under her control;
j. security and protection from threat of fear to do or not do something;
k. freedom from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity;
l. live prosperously physically and spiritually, reside and obtain a good and healthy living environment;
m. obtain health services;
n. communicate and obtain information to develop her personality and social environment;
(2) Every Woman has the right to receive empowerment in the economic, socio-cultural, political and legal fields in order to develop herself and advance herself as referred to in paragraph (1) letter e.

Article 2

The implementation of Protection for Women and Children is based on the principles of:

a. respect and recognition of equal human rights and dignity;
b. non-discrimination;
c. gender equality and justice:
d. protection of the human rights of Women and Children;
e. appreciation of the views of Children;
f. best interests of victims of violence; and
g. legal certainty.

Article 3

This Regional Regulation aims to:

a. serve as a guide in planning and implementing policies on the Protection of Women and Children;
b. prevent violations of the rights of Women and Children;
c. realize integrated, comprehensive and sustainable efforts for the Protection of Women and Children;
d. prevent decisions and policies that violate and do not support efforts for the Protection of Women and Children; and
e. increase the role of the Regency Government, community, and other community institutions in efforts to Protect Women and Children.

Part Three Community

Article 28

(1) The Community is obliged and responsible to participate in organizing the Protection of Women and Children.

(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be implemented through:

a. forming Family partners at the sub-district and village levels;
b. establishing units for the Protection of Women and Children within community organizations;
e. conducting socialization and education about the rights of Women and Children independently;
d. preventing violations of the rights of Women and Children;
e. providing first aid to Women and Children who become victims of acts of violence; and
f. providing information or reporting to the authorized agency if acts of Violence against Women and Children occur in their environment.
(3) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be implemented by individuals or groups, academics, observers of Women and Children, community-based integrated child protection, community organizations/community institutions/religious institutions/other legitimate institutions.

Article 31

The organization of the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence is implemented through:

a. complaint, consultation, and counseling services;
b. assistance services;
c. medical rehabilitation services;
d. social rehabilitation services;
e. legal services; and
f. social reintegration services.

Article 20

Every Child has the right to obtain Protection from:

a. abuse in political activities;
b. involvement in armed conflict;
c. involvement in social unrest;
d. involvement in events containing elements of Violence and discrimination;
e. involvement in warfare; and
f. sexual crimes.

Article 4

The scope of this Regional Regulation is as follows:

a. rights of Women and Children;
b. obligations and responsibilities;
c. administration of Protection for Women and Children;
d. guidance and supervision; and
e. financing;

Article 30

The organization of the Protection of Women and Children is implemented through efforts of:

a. prevention;
b. vulnerability risk reduction;
c. handling; and
d. rehabilitation.

Article 6

Women's Empowerment in the economic field as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (2) may be carried out through:

a. provision of skills and job training;
b. facilitation of the formation of productive economic business groups;
c. facilitation of strengthening and development of productive economic business groups;
d. facilitation and capital assistance; and
e. facilitation of marketing network development.

